{"timestamp": 1779347884.1491158, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 9, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779347884.1495178, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 9, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779347895.1843615, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Alice's body right in the middle of Medbay. \n\nHere is exactly what I saw before I found her: Early in the round, I was in Medbay and Alice walked in from Electrical. Shortly after, Bob came up from Storage and joined us there. I left the two of them alive in Medbay and went to Electrical to do a task. When I circled back to Medbay just now, Alice was dead. \n\nBob, you were the last person I saw in the room with her. You have a lot of explaining to do. Everyone else, let's hear where you were, but I'm looking very closely at Bob right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779347908.94139, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I was on the complete opposite side of the map from the murder. I went from Security over to Navigation to work on my tasks. Diana actually came into Navigation from Security about halfway through the round (around tick 7), and she's been in there with me ever since. \n\nBecause we were both on the far right side of the ship, I think Diana and I are completely clear of this Medbay kill, and I can vouch for her whereabouts for the latter part of the round. \n\nFrank's timeline makes a lot of sense and puts the spotlight squarely on Bob. Bob, you definitely need to explain why you were the last one seen with Alice. Also, we haven't heard anything about Charlie's whereabouts yet, so we need to figure out where he was during all of this. Let's hear from Bob next."}}
{"timestamp": 1779347922.8545427, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve, to answer your question, I was isolated on the top-left side of the ship this entire round. I started in Oxygen, finished up there, and then moved down to Upper Engine. I actually haven't seen a single person all game, so unfortunately I don't have any visual clears to provide. \n\nSince I was right next door in Upper Engine and didn't see anyone cross over, whoever killed Alice in Medbay either vented, stayed in the central area, or moved back towards Storage or Electrical. \n\nFrank, that is a highly specific and damning timeline. If you really left Bob alone with Alice in Medbay, then Bob is undoubtedly our prime suspect. But we do need to be careful of a potential self-report and frame-job from Frank. \n\nBob, we absolutely need to hear your side of the story right now. Were you in Medbay with Alice and Frank? And Diana, please confirm if you can vouch for Eve in Navigation like she claims. I'm holding my vote until I hear from the last two."}}
{"timestamp": 1779347938.4431562, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank is telling the truth about us being in Medbay, but he's conveniently leaving out the fact that I didn't stay there! Almost immediately after Frank walked out towards Electrical, I headed north into the Cafeteria, and then moved over to Weapons to do my asteroids task. I left Alice perfectly fine and alive.\n\nThink about this critically, guys: Frank admits he was in the room with Alice, claims he left for Electrical where he was completely alone, and then just so happens to \"circle back\" and find her dead? No one can vouch for him being in Electrical. Charlie is right to be cautious \u2014 this is a textbook self-report and frame job. Frank waited for me to leave for Cafeteria, killed Alice himself, and reported the body to set me up since he knew I was the last one seen there. \n\nI'm not going to let you frame me for your kill, Frank. My vote is going straight to you. Diana, let's hear your clear for Eve, but I think we have our killer right here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779347956.2654467, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "\"I can absolutely confirm Eve's alibi. I saw her in Security early on (around tick 3), and then I was with her in Navigation for the rest of the round. Eve and I are completely clear. \n\nCharlie's story makes sense since he was isolated on the left side. This means it is strictly between Frank and Bob. We have a classic 1v1 scenario. Bob, you claim you went to Weapons after Cafeteria, but I actually started my round in Weapons and moved down through Security, and I never crossed paths with you at all on the right side of the ship. \n\nBecause Frank reported the body and Bob's pathing doesn't quite line up with what I saw, I'm more inclined to believe Frank here. This is a 5-player scenario with 1 Duck left, so we have the numbers to take a shot at this 1v1. I'm voting for Bob today. If the game doesn't end, we know Frank pulled a massive frame job and we vote him next.\""}}
{"timestamp": 1779347972.4760997, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, nice try trying to turn this around on me with that desperate frame-job. You claim you went from Cafeteria to Weapons, but Diana's pathing completely dismantles your alibi. She was on that side of the map and didn't cross paths with you at all. You were the last one I saw with Alice, and now you're lying to the crew about where you went after I left the room. \n\nSince Diana and Eve are clearing each other on the right side, and Charlie was isolated on the left, it's a direct 1v1 between us. Your fabricated story about Weapons proves you're the Duck. Everyone, let's get Bob out of here."}}
